                <pb facs="0691" n="606" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg606"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.6363/488</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Mexican Embassy to the Department of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-07-21"><hi rendition="#italic">July 21,
                        1919</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>[A copy of the following telegram from the Mexican Acting Secretary of State for
                    Foreign Affairs to the Mexican Ambassador, was left at the Department by the
                    Ambassador on July 22.]</p>
                <p>Referring to your message on the subject: You may inform the Government of the
                    United States that the Mexican Government will authorize the temporary boring of
                    oil wells provided that the interested parties make application to the
                    Department of Industry and Commerce asking for such permits under the formal
                    promise that they will be subject to legislative regulations that may be enacted
                    in the future by the Mexican Government. The Department of Industry and Commerce
                    will issue at once a circular relative to this matter.</p>
                <closer>(Signed) Chief Clerk of the Department of Foreign Relations.<lb/><signed><hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">Diego Fernandez</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
